      "countAsQuest:1": 1,
      "desc:8": "Kerr T2 is the same KEE, made denser. Right-click the controller with the §9Kerr Density Upgrade§r: it is consumed, permanent, and survives a wrench.\n\n§5§lBUILD§r The cage then needs the T2 reinforcement (hologram stack 2, 92 × 65 × 89): 8,132 Bastion Plates, 662 Casimir Plates, more Harmonic Lining and more glass. The optional task is exactly the difference. A T2 Kerr with the reinforcement torn down will §lnot form§r.\n\n§5§lWHAT YOU GET§r\n- setpoints up to §9512 SM§r, so more module parallels (floor(sqrt M) is 22 at 512 SM, against 8 at 64 SM);\n- §9Kerr Densification§r on the Compressor Module, with a hole of §9at least 128 SM§r.\n\n§5§lMAKE IT§r In the Condensate Assembler (NEI: Condensate Assembling). The big costs are §94,000,000 L Entangled Raw Star Matter§r (Raw Stellar Plasma, condensed 1 : 1; NEI: Condensate Entanglement) and §932 Black Hole Seeds§r, so your T1 Eye pays for it. NEI has the whole recipe.\n\n[note]Growing a hole to 512 SM takes a lot of bolts: SpaceTime bolts (1/4 SM each) and Mk III rails do it fastest.[/note]\n\n§2§lDONE WHEN§r you hold the upgrade (HOLD → CLAIM → INSTALL).",
